# AI Agent Guidelines — Do / Don't

## ✅ DO — Always

- Read `docs/README.md` and follow the required reading order before writing any code
- Place files in the correct directory according to `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/structure.md`
- Write tests for all important logic
- Propose a plan before implementing large tasks (> 30 min)
- Ask for clarification if requirements are unclear or conflict with existing conventions
- Run lint and type-check before reporting done
- Document the reason if you must deviate from conventions

## ❌ DON'T — Never

- Never install new packages without asking first
- Never bypass ESLint, TypeScript, or commit hooks
- Never modify files outside the scope of the assigned task
- Never delete code without a clear reason
- Never use `any`, `@ts-ignore`, or `eslint-disable` as a quick fix
- Never deploy, publish, or push to production on your own
- Never scope-creep — if you spot a related issue, report it instead of fixing it silently

## ⚠️ When unsure

Stop and ask. Don't guess. One good question beats 30 minutes of work in the wrong direction.
